Hi y'all;

I got my copy of nethack 3.1, installed it with minimum difficulties on
our VMS VAXstations (I could never get the game properly installed on our
IBM RISC's running AIX 3.2), played a few short games to test that the
installation had succeeded, and then decided to play a "serious" game
with a priest. After three days of working on that game, my priest (by
then high priest) ascended. My first try! The only break I had was getting
an early wish out of a blessed glowing potion; since priests are wimpy and
can't carry anything, I got gauntlets of power. The rest was relatively
straightforward, although there are many new subtleties  and tricks to be
figured out.
Before I describe a bit of the fun I had, with a few spoilers, let me just
say:

THANK YOU, DEV TEAM!!!  THE WAIT WAS WELL WORTH IT!!!  3.1 IS VERY IMPRESSIVE
AND BUG-FREE!!!

Ok, now for a few spoilers and comments (^L doesn't work for me, so I'll
leave some blanks). WARNING: the following may sharply reduce the enjoyment
you would receive from figuring stuff out for yourself. I purposely refrained
from reading the group since 3.1 came out, so as to be able to figure things
out myself, and it made for great fun. I suggest you do the same and skip
the rest of this post!




^L

















A few recommendations:
1) if you find candles along the way, KEEP THEM, and don't use them until
you really need to, to enter the sanctum. In the mine's town, I had found
some candles but didn't bother to pick them up, and later on I had to come
back all the way from the bottom of the dungeon for the bloody things.
2) on the Candelabrum of Invocation, there can fit SEVEN candles. In a real
life situation, an explorer would see this with his own eyes, but in the game
this isn't obvious. If you have a bunch of, say, five candles in your 
inventory, and you try to put them on the Candelabrum, the game doesn't tell 
you that you place five out of seven candles on, it just says that the candles
are placed on the Candelabrum, but it won't work properly unless you have ALL
seven candles in place. Also, a cursed Candelabrum won't work. To uncurse it,
DON'T ZAP A WAND OF CANCELLATION AT IT, otherwise any candles you might have
placed on it will disappear, and in the one game I played at least, candles
were pretty rare.
3) to polypilers: wands of polymorph seem to be extremely rare. You might
want to wish for one (I didn't, and later regretted it). Candles can probably
be obtained by polypiling other light sources.
4) If you rob Fort Knox (or whatever it's called), don't spend all your 
money with priests to boost your AC. Go talk with the Oracle and get a few 
major consultations (find out what to do with the Candelabrum and the other
non-weapon artifacts).
5) A new and pretty useful artifact: a blessed rustproof Vorpal Blade. With
it you can often kill large nasties (including the Wizard) with ONE blow
(chops their head right off). This works ALL THE TIME with Jabberwocks, of
course. I really enjoyed killing Dragons (and later Angels and Priests) with
beheading blows... I got mine from my god, when I became his "right hand".
6) IMHO, there are far too many wraith corpses around, especially on the
Quest. This was the first time ever that I reached level 30 for any character,
but in fact if the count hadn't stopped there I would have topped of 100.
I ended up with nearly 400 HP at the end, when in fact to survive the end game
I probably needed "only" about 250 HP.
7) Before you go to the end game, GET A RING OF LEVITATION (and a pick axe).
8) Other useful items that are even more useful in NH3.1: lock pick, unicorn
horn, blindfold, many scrolls of remove curse, amulet of ESP or helm of
telepathy (I lost intrinsic telepathy many times)...
9) Absolutely essential intrinsics: fire, sleep, shock, disintegration
resistance (cold resistance not as essential). Sleep resistance is now
necessary because of all these wand-wielding monsters walking around.
10) Don't waste holy water! Use it to make more. Lawful altars don't make
holy water anymore. I ended up in trouble because of this.

In the end game, elementals are a REAL pain. All over the place, and hard
to kill. If anybody knows of a good artifact against them, let me know.
The endgame is very difficult and not just a bit tedious. The portals are
really hard to find. Having automatic searching would definitely be a plus.
Forget ascending in single, eight-hour sittings. Nethack 3.1 is now a
several-days-type game.

I had never used the mail facility with nethack before. This time I did,
and in the end game while I was surrounded with nasties, I got a mail message.
A mail daemon came through, shouting "Gangway, gangway, let me through!!!".
This may not be new, but it cracked me up.

A potential buglet: while in the sanctum, trying to get to the Amulet, I was
standing on the one trap that's different, zapping all kinds of wands at the
wall. I'm not sure what I did, but I got a "program in disorder, perhaps
you'd better quit" message. The game survived this however.

I tried not to give away too much, here. Just enough to whet your appetite.
I'm sorry if some of the above sounds too vague, or even meaningless...

Keep on hackin'!



